==Galician==
[[File:O Teixadal de Casaio.jpg |thumb|Pena Surbia (2116 m) and Pena Trevinca (2127 m), highest mountains in Galicia]]
[[File:Pradorramisquedo.jpg |thumb|''Vivir na montaña'' ("living in the highlands"), Pradorramisquedo, Ourense]]

===Etymology===
From Old Galician and {{inh|gl|roa-opt|montanna}} (13th century, ''{{w|Cantigas de Santa Maria}}''), from non-standard {{inh|gl|LL|montania||mountain}}, a substantivization of the feminine of {{m|LL|montanius||mountainous}}, itself a 'vulgar' alteration of Classical {{inh|gl|la|montānus}}, from {{m|la|mōns||mountain}}, from {{der|gl|ine-pro|*men-}}. Cognate with {{cog|pt|montanha}} and {{cog|es|montaña}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|[monˈtaɲɐ]}}

===Noun===
{{gl-noun|f}}

# [[highlands]]
#* '''1853''', J. M. Pintos, ''A Gaita Gallega'', page 58:
#*: ''Alá de donde vimos na '''montaña''' a miseria é tan grande que non pode a xente se queixar ''
#*:: There, where we came from, in the '''highlands''', misery is so large that people can't even complain
# [[mountain]]

